{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_202605230633456d2ac83efa774cc8","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"glm-5.1","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now I understand the flow:\n1. `swap()` is called → calls `useMove()` at line 188\n2. After all processing, `_afterMove()` is called\n3. `_afterMove()` calls `checkState()` at line 399\n\nSo `useMove()` is called BEFORE the swap, which means:\n- When remaining = 1 (29 moves used out of 30), `useMove()` increments to 30, remaining = 0, returns true\n- The swap happens, cascades process\n- `checkState()` is called → `isGameOver()` checks `remaining <= 0` → `0 <= 0` → true\n- If goal not complete → game over\n\nThis is actually correct behavior! After using the last move, if the goal isn't met, game should be over.\n\nBut wait, there's a subtle issue. Looking at `useMove()`:\n```javascript\nuseMove() {\n    this.moves++;\n    if (this.onMovesChange) this.onMovesChange(this.getRemainingMoves());\n    return this.getRemainingMoves() >= 0;\n}\n```\n\nThe return value is checked before the move, so `useMove()` allows the move when remaining >= 0 AFTER incrementing. After the move, remaining is 0. Then `isGameOver()` triggers at remaining <= 0.\n\nBut what if a player has 0 remaining moves already? Then `useMove()` would increment moves, remaining = -1, return false. The move is blocked. But the score system already incremented moves! This is a side effect bug - the move counter gets incremented even though the move is rejected.\n\nWait, looking at line 188:\n```javascript\nif (!this.scoreSystem.useMove()) return;\n```\nIf `useMove()` returns false, the swap doesn't happen. But `this.moves` was already incremented. So the moves counter is wrong.\n\nActually, that's probably not a real issue because if remaining is already 0 or negative, the game should have already ended via `checkState()`. The player shouldn't be able to make a move.\n\nLet me reconsider the \"步数边界\" bug. Looking at the issue again:\n\nThe bug might be that when remaining = 0, the cascade is still in progress but `isGameOver()` returns true. But looking at the code flow:\n1. `useMove()` is called at the start of the swap\n2. After all cascades and animations, `_afterMove()` is called\n3. `_afterMove()` calls `checkState()`\n\nSo `checkState()` is only called AFTER all cascades are done. This means the last move's cascades have fully resolved before `isGameOver()` is checked. So this shouldn't be the issue.\n\nActually, let me look at this more carefully. In `_afterMove()`:\n```javascript\nthis.state = STATES.IDLE;\nif (!this.board.hasValidMoves(this.obstacleMgr)) {\n  this.board.shuffle();\n}\nthis.scoreSystem.checkState();\n```\n\nThe shuffle happens BEFORE `checkState()`. If the board has no valid moves and shuffles, then `checkState()` runs. This seems fine.\n\nWait, I just realized something. The `checkState()` in `ScoreSystem`:\n```javascript\ncheckState() {\n    if (this.isGoalComplete()) {\n      if (this.onLevelComplete) this.onLevelComplete(this.score, this.getStarCount());\n      return 'complete';\n    }\n    if (this.isGameOver()) {\n      if (this.onLevelFail) this.onLevelFail(this.score);\n      return 'fail';\n    }\n    return 'playing';\n  }\n```\n\nAnd `isGameOver()`:\n```javascript\nisGameOver() {\n    return this.getRemainingMoves() <= 0 && !this.isGoalComplete();\n}\n```\n\nHmm, what about boss levels? `isGoalComplete()` returns `false` for boss type (line 175). So on a boss level, after using all moves, `isGoalComplete()` is false, and `isGameOver()` returns true. But the boss might have been defeated during the cascade! The boss defeat is handled externally.\n\nLet me check how boss defeat is handled.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"efc4c585-24c5-4fd5-bbba-79c262b1755c","uuid":"603964ae-d455-43aa-a985-ea535cced8d6"}
