= -(writeRow - r + 1) * tileSize - r * tileSize = -(writeRow + 1) * tileSize`\n- This seems correct actually — the new tile starts above the board at the right pixel offset. Let me reconsider...\n- Actually, the problem report says: \"Board.applyGravity 填充新 tile 时 tile.offsetY = -(writeRow - r + 1) 用的是格子数单位，但 Game._processChain 中重力动画用像素偏移 fromRow * tileSize\"\n- But since Game.js immediately overwrites tile.offsetY with the correct pixel value, this bug might not actually manifest. The Board.js offsetY value is immediately overwritten.\n- Hmm, but looking at _removeAndCascade (line 522-523), it calls `this.board.applyGravity()` but doesn't set up animations for the drops! It just calls `applyGravity()` and ignores the return value.\n- Wait no, in _processChain line 355-363, the drops are handled correctly with animations. And _removeAndCascade line 522-523 doesn't handle animations for gravity at all. That's a different issue.\n\nOK, I think BUG-4 might be a non-issue since Game.js overwrites the offsetY. But the initial tile.offsetY from Board.js could cause a brief visual glitch if the renderer reads it before Game.js sets the animation. Let me just make Board.js consistent by not setting offsetY at all (since Game.js handles it).\n\nActually, looking at the _removeAndCascade code (lines 482-528), it calls `this.board.applyGravity()` at line 522 but does NOT process the drops array to set up animations! This means after rainbow or other special triggers, the gravity animation won't play properly. That's a real bug!\n\nLet me plan my fixes:\n\n**BUG-4 fix**: Make Board.js applyGravity not set offsetY (since Game.js handles it). Also fix _removeAndCascade to properly animate gravity drops.\n\n**BUG-5 fix**: After creating special tiles, auto-trigger their effects. But the report says this might be by design. Let me just leave it as-is or add a config option.\n\n**BUG-6 fix**: In Characters.js, after setting hp=0, also remove from obstacles array or call the proper destruction method.\n\n**BUG-7 fix**: The canvas click handler in index.html handles clicks during Navigation screens and the back button. The InputHandler handles mousedown/mouseup for swipe. These shouldn't overlap because InputHandler checks if enabled (only during IDLE state), and the click handler checks Navigation first. But the issue is that a swipe can also trigger a click event. The fix is to prevent the click handler from processing board interactions (it only handles navigation and back button).\n\nActually wait - looking more carefully, the canvas click handler in index.html doesn't handle board interactions (no swap/move logic). It handles: ad overlay clicks, navigation clicks, and back-to-map button. The InputHandler handles board interactions via mousedown/mouseup. These are actually different event types and shouldn't conflict much. The main concern is that a swipe (mousedown+mousemove+mouseup) could also trigger a click event on some browsers, but since the click handler doesn't do board moves, this shouldn't cause double processing.\n\nLet me reconsider - the report says \"InputHandler 绑定了 mousedown/mouseup 事件处理棋盘操作，但 index.html 的 canvas click handler 也可能触发相同事件\". Looking at the code, the click handler in index.html only handles ad overlay, navigation, and back button. The InputHandler handles board moves. These are different concerns, so BUG-7 might be a false alarm. But to be safe, I can prevent click events on the canvas when InputHandler processes a swipe.\n\n**BUG-8 fix**: Implement tap-to-select-then-tap-adjacent-to-swap in _handleTap.\n\nLet me now proceed with the fixes. Let me also read a few more files.\n\nActually, let me just fix the most impactful bugs and move on to the Douyin submission prep since that's the main goal. Let me prioritize:\n\n1. BUG-4: Fix _removeAndCascade to animate gravity (P0)\n2. BUG-6: Fix obstacle removal in Characters.js (P1)\n3. BUG-7: Prevent click/swipe conflict (P1)\n4. BUG-8: Implement tap-to-select interaction (P1)\n5. BUG-5: Skip this one as it may be by design (P1)\n\nPlus P2 fixes:\n6. BUG-9: Update levels.js comment\n7. BUG-10: Remove unused level JSON files\n8. BUG-11: Extract _roundRect to shared utility (too much refactoring, skip)\n9. BUG-14: Add sound toggle UI\n10. Remove console.log from Analytics.js\n\nThen Douyin prep:\n- Create project.config.json\n- Create game.json\n- Add meta tags\n- Verify package size\n- Remove .codegraph/ and levels/ JSON\n\nLet me start fixing.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ec73960d-df44-45f4-a48b-a11bb93a968e","uuid":"ebaa4ac3-2e78-4ae9-b3d7-5669a494812b"}
